sted: TC-342, TC-343). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes.","+- 2026-10-09 — refresh under approval. Copied: low-level-requirements.toml (re-attested: LLR-047, LLR-320); test-cases.toml (re-attested: TC-342, TC-343). Registries not named by this act keep their prior snapshot bytes."]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":524,"oldLines":3,"newStart":524,"newLines":9,"lines":[" date = \"2026-10-09\""," approved = []"," reattested = [\"TC-342\", \"TC-343\"]","+","+[[act]]","+seq = 87","+date = \"2026-10-09\"","+approved = []","+reattested = [\"LLR-047\", \"LLR-320\", \"TC-342\", \"TC-343\"]"]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":501,"oldLines":7,"newStart":501,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Run capability menu reader\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/run_menu.py;project-trajectory/scripts/run.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/run.template.cmd;project-trajectory/scripts/run.template.command\""," code_symbol = \"load_capabilities/interactive_menu/direct/launch\"","-detail = \"load_capabilities parses the docs/stack.ini [run] section (configparser, interpolation=None, case-preserving optionxform; declaration order kept; a name.desc row attaches to its command and an orphan or empty-value command is dropped) into an ordered (name, command, desc) list; --list prints name<TAB>desc per row; direct(name) launches by exact-match name (exit 2 on an unknown name) and launch() runs the shell line via subprocess shell=True, passing the child exit code straight through; interactive_menu prints the numbered menu, reads a pick from stdin, and returns EOF-safe without hanging; an absent or empty [run] prints guidance and exits 1. The no-argument run launchers change to the repository root and invoke dev-setup's --for-run/-ForRun readiness operation once before the menu; a nonzero result prints guidance and leaves the menu unopened. Direct and --list forms bypass that operation and, on Windows, the closing pause; run.command delegates to run.sh so it does not duplicate the operation, and non-interactive menu input remains available after it.\"","+detail = \"load_capabilities parses the docs/stack.ini [run] section (configparser, interpolation=None, case-preserving optionxform; declaration order kept; a name.desc row attaches to its command and an orphan or empty-value command is dropped) into an ordered (name, command, desc) list; --list prints name<TAB>desc per row; direct(name) launches by exact-match name (exit 2 on an unknown name) and launch() runs the shell line via subprocess shell=True, passing the child exit code straight through; interactive_menu prints the numbered menu, reads a pick from stdin, and returns EOF-safe without hanging; an absent or empty [run] prints guidance and exits 1. Every run launcher form resolves one interpreter by running, in order, its repository virtual-environment candidates and then the candidates from its dev-setup's ordinary runtime search, taking the first that reports Python 3.11 or later as its executable path; it runs the menu on exactly that path. The no-argument launchers change to the repository root and invoke dev-setup's --for-run/-ForRun readiness operation once before the menu, handing it that interpreter when one resolves; a nonzero result prints guidance and leaves the menu unopened. Direct and --list forms bypass that operation and, on Windows, the closing pause, and exit 1 with guidance when no interpreter resolves; run.command delegates to run.sh so it does not duplicate the operation, and non-interactive menu input remains available after it.\""," rationale = \"\"\"The command being run is the user's own declared line, so shell=True is the same trust boundary the declaration already establishes rather than a new one. EOF-safety is load-bearing: a menu that blocks on a closed stdin turns an unattended invocation into a hang, which is the failure this launcher exists to avoid.\"\"\""," test_refs = \"(see TC-047; TC-342)\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":3402,"oldLines":7,"newStart":3402,"newLines":7,"lines":[" title = \"Dev-setup readiness operation for a bare run\""," module = \"project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.sh;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.ps1;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.cmd;project-trajectory/scripts/dev-setup.template.command\""," code_symbol = \"detect_runtime/interactive/maybe_install;FindPython/Interactive/MaybeInstall\"","-detail = \"The --for-run/-ForRun operation reports workstation readiness first, then offers each missing setup item only at an interactive terminal; without one it offers nothing and does not consume menu input. It exits 0 when the runtime is ready after the offers and otherwise exits 1 with the step to take. The standalone --check/-Check operation reports only, performs no offer or write, and exits 0.\"","+detail = \"The --for-run/-ForRun operation reports workstation readiness first, then offers each missing setup item only at an interactive terminal; without one it offers nothing and does not consume menu input. Its runtime is the interpreter the launcher hands it, never one it searches for: it exits 0 when that interpreter satisfies the runtime floor and otherwise, including when none is handed, exits 1 with the step to take. The standalone --check/-Check operation reports only, performs no offer or write, and exits 0.\""," rationale = \"A menu can be useful only after its runtime is usable, but the readiness step must not turn a piped or automated launch into an unattended installer.\""," test_refs = \"TC-343\""," status = \"Approved\""]}]},{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml","hunks":[{"oldStart":3477,"oldLines":22,"newStart":3477,"newLines":22,"lines":[" [test.TC-342]"," verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"SR-046\", \"IF-157\", \"IF-158\", \"IF-292\", \"LLR-047\", \"IF-293\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run bare, direct and list launchers against a scaffold and the repository with varied readiness results.\"","+method = \"Run bare, direct and list launchers against a scaffold and the repository with varied readiness results, observing the interpreter handed to the readiness step and the one the menu runs on, and with only sub-floor interpreters first on PATH; compare each launcher's candidate list with its dev-setup's runtime search.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"A bare run checks once before its menu and stops on a missing runtime; direct and list forms do not check or pause.\"","+expected = \"A bare run checks once before its menu, handing the check the interpreter the menu then runs on, and stops on a missing runtime; direct and list forms do not check or pause; with no Python 3.11+ interpreter no form starts the menu; each launcher searches the same interpreters, in the same order, as its dev-setup.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_never_call_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_of_run_cmd_never_check_or_pause; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_run_shows_its_menu_after_the_check\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_never_call_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_calls_the_check_once_from_the_root_before_the_menu; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_direct_and_list_forms_of_run_cmd_never_check_or_pause; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_this_repos_run_shows_its_menu_after_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_hands_the_check_the_interpreter_its_menu_runs_on; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_no_form_of_run_starts_the_menu_below_the_floor; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_each_run_launcher_searches_what_its_dev_setup_searches\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "," [test.TC-343]"," verifies = [\"SR-032\", \"LLR-320\"]"," level = \"Integration\"","-method = \"Run the readiness operation with interactive and non-interactive input, a missing runtime, and piped menu input; also run the standalone check. At a terminal, drive each missing-item offer through consent; drive standalone check at a terminal.\"","+method = \"Run the readiness operation with interactive and non-interactive input, a missing runtime, and piped menu input; also run the standalone check. At a terminal, drive each missing-item offer through consent; drive standalone check at a terminal. Run the readiness operation with and without a handed interpreter while a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH.\""," tier = \"Full\"","-expected = \"The operation reports before offering, offers nothing without a terminal, preserves piped menu input, and exits with guidance when the runtime remains missing; standalone check is read-only and exits 0. At a terminal each missing item is offered consent-first, while standalone check offers and writes nothing.\"","+expected = \"The operation reports before offering, offers nothing without a terminal, preserves piped menu input, and exits with guidance when the runtime remains missing; standalone check is read-only and exits 0. At a terminal each missing item is offered consent-first, while standalone check offers and writes nothing. Without a handed interpreter it reports the runtime missing and exits 1 although a Python 3.11+ interpreter is on PATH; with one that satisfies the floor it exits 0.\""," automated = \"Yes\"","-evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_each_missing_item_is_offered_consent_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_standalone_check_at_a_terminal_offers_and_writes_nothing\"","+evidence = \"tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_offers_nothing_without_a_terminal; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_piped_menu_input_survives_the_check; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_a_bare_run_cmd_stops_with_the_step_when_the_runtime_stays_missing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_at_a_terminal_each_missing_item_is_offered_consent_first; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_standalone_check_at_a_terminal_offers_and_writes_nothing; tests/test_run_devsetup.py::test_the_check_for_run_checks_only_the_interpreter_it_is_handed\""," status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-834\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\test\\test-cases.toml"]}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsNPYgsPsXs6JjzaQGhq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four amended rows change meaning, and I blessed and re-attested every one. The verdict is `f5c95e87` and the re-attestation is `029a5a08`. Both end with `WI: WI-834` and passed the commit hooks. The snapshot copied the LLR and TC registries without refusal.\n\nThe four rows describe one design change: the run launcher picks a single Python 3.11+ interpreter, hands it to dev-setup's readiness check, and runs the menu on that same interpreter. The check no longer searches for a runtime of its own. This answers review 012 F1.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=4`.**\n- **LLR-047:** every launcher form now picks the interpreter by actually running each candidate: the repo's `.venv` first, then dev-setup's own list. The direct and list forms now exit 1 with guidance when nothing qualifies. Both changes are new obligations.\n- **LLR-320:** the readiness check (`--for-run`) now uses only the interpreter it is handed, and exits 1 without one even if a 3.11+ Python is on PATH. That changes where the runtime comes from and when the check succeeds.\n- **TC-342 and TC-343:** each adds test cases pinning that design: the handed interpreter is the menu's, no form starts below the 3.11 floor, the launchers search the same list as dev-setup, and the check uses only what it is handed.\n\n**What I checked:**\n- Both launcher templates and both dev-setup templates match the new text.\n- The run/dev-setup, evidence-join and run-menu suites gave `68 passed, 5 skipped`. The skips are three cases that need a terminal Windows lacks, one POSIX-only case and one known Windows limit.\n- All four new tests the TCs cite ran on this host and passed, across both launcher families.\n\n**One behaviour change to know about:** if someone installs Python through dev-setup's offer during a bare run, the run now ends with \"run again\" instead of opening the menu. I accepted this. The launcher picked its interpreter before the install, and a fresh install is often not on the running shell's PATH anyway. SR-046's \"if the runtime remains missing\" reasonably means no runtime the launcher can run on.\n\nThe `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":441514,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":731},"output_tokens":703,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"66057f07-f0ef-45e9-a17a-d8a8ca84bcc1","timestamp":"2026-10-09T21:25:44.285Z","request_id":"req_011CfsNPYMX57rYHQhvtqmts"}
